  "Question": "What does the denominator of a fraction represent?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "The number of equal parts into which the whole is divided",
    "B": "The number of parts taken",
    "C": "The total number of wholes"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The denominator represents the number of equal parts into which the whole is divided, so the answer is A. It is the numerator that represents how many of those parts are taken.",
